{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2","id":1514065,"title":"Head Canons & Home Brew Part 2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-06T15:54:16-07:00","id":1514065,"title":"Head Canons & Home Brew Part 2","content":"Bringing it back in a new form instead of necro-ing the original. (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1357074-head-canons-home-brew\">Original is here.</a>) <br /> <br /> The place for anyone to share their own ideas, alterations, or changes to the Werewolf setting. <br /> <br /> <br /> As I mentioned elsewhere, lately I've pondered the idea of Hunters in Darkness and White Howlers as alternate names for the two Native American tribes. However, as part of a wider effort to remove human-culture derived names from all of the tribes, I'm still trying to figure out what would take the place of the Fianna and Get of Fenris (as well as the Croatan and Bunyip, as well as what would be the alternate origins of the Black Spiral Dancers). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T16:24:48-07:00","id":1514067,"title":"","content":"Something I was considering that might help with that:<br /> <br /> Have &quot;Lodges&quot; that work like the Silver Fang Houses as localized versions of much broader Tribes that have associated Totem spirits, rename the Silver Fang Lodges into something else.<br /> <br /> The Fianna, canon White Howlers, Get of Fenris, and Younger Brother are all Lodges of the same Tribe (White Howlers being the original shared name works fine). Older Brother, Nuwisha, Kitsune (I know not everyone will like those), and the Bunyip (though I house rule them to the singing dogs and dingoes, not thylacines) are Lodges of the same Tribe, with the Ghost Council name being a good one IMO. Middle Brother, Stargazers, and the Shadow Lords are Lodges of the same Tribe (I like the idea that the Shadow Lords actually started in Central Asia and followed the Turkic migrations west, and Hunters in the Darkness would work as an umbrella name for these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-07-2023, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T18:04:23-07:00","id":1514070,"title":"","content":"<b>Black Furies</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>The Gorgon</i><br /> Theme: Rage for the vengeful.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, an Avenger must openly declare vengeance against someone, or alternatively, publically accept being the target of another\u2019s vengeance.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Rat</i><br /> Theme: Rage in defense of the downtrodden.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Scrapper must destroy the assets and wealth of a designated enemy, or alternatively, liquidate her own wealth.<br /> <br /> <b>Circle of Gaia</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>The Unicorn</i><br /> Theme: Rage against defilement of purity.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Paladin must destroy a Triatic spirit, or alternatively, use pain to atone for her own past misdeeds.<br /> <br /> <b>The Wild Hunt (replaces Fianna)</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Stag</i><br /> Theme: Rage until ecstasy and catharsis.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Horned must immerse in any intense activity where everyone else ends up losing reason, or alternatively, she is left unconscious.<br /> <br /> <b>Get of Fenris</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>The Fenris-Wolf</i><br /> Theme: Rage against the false gods.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Vargr must destroy a manifestation of religious faith (including living devotees), or alternatively, something related to her human upbringing (if any).<br /> <br /> <u>Note</u>: The Get are the Lupusborn-dominant Tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Glass Walkers</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Honeybee</i><br /> Theme: Rage until a breakthrough is found.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Hand must create something subjectively innovative, or alternatively, destroy one of her previous creations.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>The Gryphon</i><br /> Theme: Rage against oppression and suppression.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Marked must \u2026\u2026 (undetermined yet)<br /> <br /> <u>Note</u>: The Talons are the Crinosborn-dominant Tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Lords</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Grandfather Thunder</i><br /> Theme: Rage until another submits.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Condemner must seize victory without revealing herself until the outcome is sealed, or alternatively, do so while revealing every one of her steps to do such.<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Owl</i><br /> Theme: Rage to make the past remembered.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Ghost must reenact the legacy of an ancestorial figure, or alternatively, spend one full night in the deeper Underworld (called the Tempest by necromancers).<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Falcon</i><br /> Theme: Rage until inspiration is stoked.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Lordling must seize victory while leading others as a superior, or alternatively, challenge leadership from a clear superior.<br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>The Qilin</i><br /> Theme: Rage to attain clarity of mind.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Reader must \u2026\u2026 (undetermined yet)<br /> <br /> <b>River\u2019s Eye (replaces Uktena/Older Brother)</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Serpent</i><br /> Theme: Rage in defiance of the hidden.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Whistler must expose an enemy\u2019s secret, or alternatively, her own.<br /> <br /> <b>Winter\u2019s Maw (replaces Wendigo/Younger Brother)</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Brother Winter</i><br /> Theme: Rage in defense of the self and selfhood.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Devourer must consume some part of someone or something that has slighted her, or alternatively, expose herself to extreme environments harsh enough to harm her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Black Spiral Dancers</b><br /> Greater Patron Spirit: <i>Nightjar</i><br /> Theme: Rage to tear down everything.<br /> Tribute: Once per month, a Cursed must destroy a Changer or a Kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T18:15:17-07:00","id":1514071,"title":"","content":"A slightly alternate take on the Ratkin, as Gaia's Plague, meant to keep human populations in check. The initial Wars of Rage (in their case, against the Bastet as much as the Garou) wrecked them, sending them off the rails. The explosion of the human population after the end of the Impergium is believed to have driven them spiritually insane on some level.<br /> <br /> Auspices (based on the classic bodily humors, in fitting with the fact that they undergo a spiritual disease as part of the first change, and that they are more or less meant as a plague on the human world)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Sanguine</b> - Extremely extroverted and hyperactive. The most social of the Ratkin, often involved with kinfolk and those outside the nest. They frequently maintain connections between the breed around the world, and are those given the unwanted task of interacting with other changing breeds. Many of their gifts allow them to pass as normal (at least for a while), go where they aren't wanted, and convince others of absurd untruths.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>Choleric</b> - Extroverted and short-tempered. The most violent of the Ratkin, acting as fighters and killers. They defend their nest-mates with an insane ferocity, using any means necessary to win and survive. Their gifts are primarily combat oriented, but as much involving hit and run tactics, escape and evasion, and ambush as actual physical damage.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>Melancholic</b> - Extremely introverted and anxious. The most intellectual of the Ratkin, fixated on their plots and schemes. They help maintain the breed's history and lore, such as it is, and help develop plans to destroy their enemies. Their gifts are mainly focused on uncovering information, remaining undetected, and sabotage.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>Phlegmatic</b> - Introverted and cold. The creepiest of the Ratkin, mystics who delve into the secrets of decay, disease, and derangement. The religious leaders of their kind, devoted to the culling of humanity and destruction of all who have wronged them. Their gifts involve interaction with spirits, the powers of entropy, and care of their nest mates.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Contagions are widespread social subgroups of the Ratkin. (&quot;The Plague&quot; refers to the spiritual disease which infects them during the first change, spoken of in religious reverence, and so isn't used to describe something as mundane as a subculture.) Having existed as long as human civilization, they've constantly evolved and changed over the millennia, with new ones spawning and old ones falling away as the whims of time dictate.<br /> <br /> Desert Rats - Paranoid survivalists who prefer to stay isolated from the rest of the world. Their nests often resemble militia compounds or are based out of abandoned Cold War bunkers or silos. The oldest surviving nests are tribes of bandits in North Africa and Asia.<br /> <br /> Sea Rats - Cutthroat pirates who have been sailing the oceans for as long as humans have had boats. Their strongholds are often hidden islands or abandoned ships. Gangs will swarm ships, often killing everyone on board and stealing everything they can carry off.<br /> <br /> Swamp Rats - Inbred, xenophobic and often violent dwellers in swamps and wetlands.<br /> <br /> Tunnel Rats - As much explorers as survivors, they've long dwelt among the caves, catacombs and modern infrastructure of the world. Many have taken to constructing and expanding their warrens, even into the umbra.<br /> <br /> Street Rats - The most common Ratkin in the modern urban world. Members often dwell among the homeless and other street people.<br /> <br /> Pack Rats - Obsessive collectors of anything under the sun. They horde and jealously guard their treasures, often competing to have the biggest or most unique collections. Anything goes in the acquisition of thing, including theft and murder.<br /> <br /> The Rat Race - A fairly modern phenomenon, paralleling the rise of office culture and bureaucracies. Members are usually among the lowest levels of office workers, as well as janitorial staff and other invisible cogs of the modern corporate world. They work to sabotage the companies they work for.<br /> <br /> Plague Rats - An almost cult like culture devoted to the exploration and spread of disease among the human populations. They work to spread - and sometimes develop - new diseases in an effort to ultimately return the world to an Impergium like state.<br /> <br /> Lab Rats - Mad scientists and survivors of human experiments. They develop bizarre weapons and tools while waging war against human science and other enemies.<br /> <br /> Mall Rats - Spawned during the late 70s and 80s, members once spent their time crawling all over human shopping malls and other places of commerce. However, since the collapse of malls in the United States, those who remain continue to haunt the locations, long after they've been abandoned by man.<br /> <br /> Jungle Rats - Primarily rat-born, they prefer the savage jungles and forests far from humanity, carving out their own strange kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Rats in the Temple - Unique among the Ratkin of India, they are centered around the Karni Mata temple in Rajasthan. They take a slightly less antagonistic attitude toward humanity and other changing breeds, and are more focused on battling the forces of the Wyrm. Other Ratkin find them odd, if not insane.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 06-07-2023, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T23:19:03-07:00","id":1514081,"title":"","content":"In my Setting, the Red Talons fell to the Wyrm. All that hate against humans, and the actual and active intent of genocide maked them easy prey against the Wyrm. The Garou Nation is shocked, but not surprised. <br /> <br /> The Black Dancers is more a &quot;Catch them all&quot; term more than a real tribe. To the Garou, all Dancers are the same. But them know better. The subtribes or factions, are:<br /> - The Blood Talons (Ex Red Talons): To them, the Wyrm corrupted because the Weaver captured it to stop the Wyrm killing Humans. Exterminate the Humans, and the Wyrm will be free<br /> - Spiral Dancers: The Wyrm is the hero of a bad tale. He is trying to do his job, and if the Garou stop being stupid and serving a narcissitic and dying spirit, they can travel down the Spiral and help liberate the Wyrm. Free the Wyrm, and everything will be in order<br /> - Void Dreamers: This is a dream. Existence is the dream of the Wyrm, and his corruption, trails of the real world dripping to this. Gaia is dead. The Weaver is dead. Only the Wyrm, eternal but dreaming, is alive. When the Wyrm wake up, all reality will disappear. Enjoy this time, to the end, because nothing matter<br /> <br /> In my games, the Lupus are not playable, and the Metis dont have a Curse, but they are sterile anyway. All Garou can have deformities, and the prejuice against them is because of that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T00:18:16-07:00","id":1514086,"title":"","content":"This is something I've been thinking since the Howler tribebook released.<br /> <br /> Essentially, White Howlers are still around, they got the help they need from other tribes.<br /> <br /> However, Black spiral Dancers are very much a thing. As BSDs are generally a hodgepodge tribe anyway, they don't need a single tribe to fall. In fact, BSDs could build their numbers in peace as the Nation was too busy infighting.<br /> <br /> What this means is;<br /> <br /> -BSDs function like they do in revised, they are focused on freeing Father from the Weaver.<br /> -BSD purebreed behaves like normal purebreed, going from 1-5. High BSD purebreed is a greenish or purplish dark fur with glowing green or red eyes and horizontal face stripes.<br /> - Their Patron is Shrike because Whip-Poor-Will might have a creepy call but it is the definition of a muppet face. Also, because WPW is a solely American bird. Shrike asks its followers to ensure their prey die slowly and in pain.<br /> - Like in revised but more pronounced due to being made out of random garou banding together, the BSDs strongest tool is their call for unity. The Gaian tribes all argue and fight one another, there is only ONE tribe of the Wyrm! Naturally, they see themselves as a sort of brother tribe to the Children of Gaia. A comparison the Coggies are uncomfortable with.<br /> - While there are no Middle Brother among the tribe, there are some Bunyip still remaining in the Australian hives. Because the BSDs focus on recruiting garou fed up with the Nation, many Bunyip joined them. Yes, this does mean the thylacine still exists in this WoD. Though all are tainted.<br /> <br /> Main inspiration was getting to use Howlers by the TB, the fact that BSDs could easily have formed without a tribe falling AND the dumb way the BSD purebreed worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T15:44:53-07:00","id":1514139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2#post1514065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, as part of a wider effort to remove human-culture derived names from all of the tribes, I'm still trying to figure out what would take the place of the Fianna and Get of Fenris (as well as the Croatan and Bunyip, as well as what would be the alternate origins of the Black Spiral Dancers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've long been in favor of expanding the tribes beyond human culture. Tribal culture should be based around cultic devotion to their totem. I also believe all the tribal names are essentially poetic expressions, and there have been many different versions over the years. Their &quot;true&quot; name as such is probably something like &quot;Children of Stag&quot;, &quot;Children of Unicorn&quot;, &quot;Children of Rat&quot; and so on. The Garou tribes predate all human ethnic groups that exist today - when the ancient Get of Fenris were in Scandinavia around 8000 BC, they certainly weren't referring to themselves through the lens of Norse culture - the Germanic speaking peoples didn't even exist then, nor did their ancestors live there. And I've long thought that it was extremely lazy to use the totem name as the tribal name for the Uktena and Wendigo. Every other tribe gets some fancy name, but they don't? So I'm good with Ghost Council being used for the Uktena (or if you want to call the totem the Horned Serpent or Underwater Panther). It's about time they got something more poetic.<br /> <br /> The &quot;true names&quot; of any of these spirits are going to be secret anyway, so whatever name is used is only going to be used by others to identify it. It's not even as if &quot;Stag&quot; is going to be universal because that is still in English. And not even if we hire a linguist to invent the Garou Tongue will that be the &quot;true&quot; name of the spirit.<br /> <br /> However, I smell the strong whiff of some kind of Pol Pot inspired &quot;Year Zero&quot; brewing around the changes in W5 that seems to seek eradicating everything that does not fit the new philosophy (which will inevitably later be condemned by some future generation, coming sooner than the current version of the Red Guards think). So I'm not in favor of &quot;removing&quot; human-culture derived names. It is almost inevitable that homids will draw on their own human heritage when discussing their Garou culture as well. It's fine for copyright purposes or sourcebook clarity to use one dominant name for each tribe. But I would prefer to keep the original names as one of many names being used currently and historically in the setting. Let everyone feel they can use whatever name they want, and discourage the tendency for some to claim using another name is somehow &quot;wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> = =<br /> <br /> I think other names for the Fianna are very easy. Revised Fianna tribebook already gave us lots of versions - Hounds of the Horned One, Skysingers, and Night Claws. Although of these, I think only Hounds of the Horned Ones is relevant. But the term Fianna simply means a warrior band. So Soldiers of Stag work just fine if you want something alliterative and suggestive of the original name.<br /> <br /> Fenris is a bit different, because if you want to universalize the name Fenris, you need to first determine what exactly is the Fenris spirit to the Garou? It is simply a variation of the Big Bag Wolf - the most dangerous wolf that all others fear - perhaps the greatest Jaggling of Father Wolf that grew so powerful he became an Incarna of its own? Is it as the Wolf of the Apocalypse who disappeared (imprisoned, sleeping, bound - voluntarily or involuntarily, etc.) for now but whose appearance will signal the start of the Apocalypse? And early legendary Garou who became so mighty and famous he became an Incarna and assembled a tribe of his own (Hakkaken likewise became an Incarna so it is possible)? Some kind of Undeworld Wolf/Dog that guards the entrance of hell? A combination of multiple of these? Once you figure out what you think Fenris should be, it's much easier to give him an alternate name that could be used, and then different versions of Get of that Spirit would be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T15:54:02-07:00","id":1514140,"title":"","content":"Some tribal head-canons and thoughts I\u2019ve had\u2026 (Part 1)<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies</b><br /> \u2022I think the idea of replacing the chief spirit patron/totem with Gorgon is interesting but I can also see the argument for Pegasus as being part of that<br /> \u2022I think that the \u2018Furies\u2019 element of the Black Furies is useful to embrace on a few levels:<br /> -1. it allows the tribe the imo interesting thematic tendency of being the avengers of primordial laws and taboos (Kinslaying, Matricide, [improper] Cannibalism, Defilement of sacred spaces, etc.); while the focus of this has become the Patriarch as the usurper of the Matriarch\u2019s former role, it also applies to other taboos<br /> \u20141a. I think that the taboo focus creates some interesting overlap with Older Brother but I\u2019d say the difference is that OB guards/maintains taboos while the Black Furies seek out and punish violators <br /> -2. I think that the image of the \u2018Furies\u2019 allows a connection to be made with Cthonic elements (which \u2018Black\u2019 also helps with. I think it allows the tribe to establish connections with cthonic powers (Night, Plagues, Life Death Cycles [The Demeter-Hades-Persephone Drama], etc.<br /> \u2022I envision the Black Furies as having three archetypal scenes associated with them:<br /> -1. \u201cBarbarian steppes\u201d; the Furies are associated with Scythians, Amazons, and other wild-outsider peoples who lived on the periphery of the Hellenic world and their civilized compatriots (Egypt, Mesopotamia, etc.)<br /> -2. Sacred places; the Furies also guard and conceal places of power, particularly those closely aligned with primordial life forces (primeval shrines of the Earth Mother and the like). The Furies guard islands hidden in the mist, remote glades, and the hearts of deep jungles<br /> -3. Cthonic darkness; the Furies also gain power from the caverns and cave mouths where the cthonic forces can be contacted and which have connection to the more dark/cthonic side of the Mother principle <br /> \u2022The Black Furies are on the periphery of \u2018civilized\u2019 areas; they would go into the cities of the Hellenic world with mystical disguises but represented the prior order to the forces of social power the early polities harnessed to distinguish themselves from the old mother-cults and primordial societies <br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers</b><br /> \u2022The Bone Gnawers do not have any one particular origin but are originally composed of Garou and their kinfolk who were outcast from their societies of origin for a variety of reasons and causes (being Garou-born, being cowards, being criminals, being taboo-breakers, being disabled, being too old, etc.); the earliest Bone Gnawers scraped to survive and would eventually come under the auspices of the Scavenger Kings (Rat, Jackal, Crow, Vulture, Coyote, etc.)<br /> \u2022The auspices of the Scavenger Kings is why the Bone Gnawers have lost their ancestor spirits and pure breed; they have forsaken their old taboos and been broken off from the old communities of spirit they came from and have become united by the pragmatic egalitarian-survivor principle of the scavengers <br /> \u2022The Bone Gnawers have developed a historical connection with outsiders and outcasts but with Rat\u2019s focus in particular being on survival and the importance of survival - one doesn\u2019t necessarily need to fight direct battles as long as they fight to survive<br /> \u2022The Bone Gnawers are historically the Garou who would remain somewhere after taint had overwhelmed it - this is for instance the case for why Bone Gnawers took over traditionally Silent Strider septs after their cataclysmic confrontation with the Cult of Seth; this is also why modern Bone Gnawers are so often found in cities<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia</b><br /> \u2022Black Fox has a good thread about Unicorn that I\u2019ve taken inspiration from for how I handle the Children of Gaia<br /> \u2022The Children of Gaia are a leadership tribe like the Silver Fangs or Shadow Lords; the Unicorns believe in the necessity of a restoration of a pure and undivided Garou and that the whole of the Nation must be reunited under a single great tribe (whether the appropriate totem for this tribe is Mother Life [Gaia], Wolf, or Unicorn is a matter of debate)<br /> \u2022The Children of Gaia will accept any members who are willing to undertake pledges to their principles and cleansing, which is why they\u2019ve maintained their Ancestors and Pure Breed while other tribes who have broadly opened their ranks have not<br /> \u2022The Children of Gaia has a number of camps dedicated to uniting various groups (Humanity &amp; Garou, Human Groups, Humans &amp; Wolves, Garou Groups, Humanity &amp; Spirits, etc.); the ideal of the tribe is the eventual restoration of all the world into the harmonious Circle of Mother (Gaia) which they believe was the original and primordial state","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T17:12:34-07:00","id":1514146,"title":"","content":"I've always associated the Black Furies with the larger Ancient Greek world, including the Black Sea region (modern Turkey, Ukraine, the Caucasus), Syria, parts of the Balkans, Italy, and the various islands of the eastern Mediterranean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:04:56-07:00","id":1514219,"title":"","content":"Some more tribal head canons and thoughts (Part 2)\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022In general: I think that what many tribes do is that they are particularly prominent examples of what all or most Garou do; for example the Fianna are not the only Garou that have sexual relations/unions with spirits but they are particularly notable for it <br /> <br /> <b>Fianna (Horned Ones)</b><br /> \u2022Compare/Contrast the Fianna with the Fenrir below<br /> \u2022The Fianna are the tribe which most highlights communal ties with their kinfolk; Fianna are deeply invested with familial links (both by blood and ritual custom), hospitality, communal honor, etc; more than any other tribe Stag emphasizes the importance of family (due to Stag\u2019s position as a Patriarch and icon fertility/virility/pride) and so Fianna are closely involved <br /> \u2022Stag as a totem for the Fianna represents Virility, Pride, Fertility, Family, Passion, Experience, Fecundity, Generosity, Natural, etc.<br /> \u2022Stag is associated with nature and the wilderness like most Garou totems are; but in particular Stag is associated with the virility, fecundity, and heaving excess of life which gives the Fianna their reputation for excessive love of life, insatiable sexual appetites, teeming hordes of children, clannish pride for their relations, proud boasting and rivalry (Stags bellowing and clashing antlers), etc.<br /> \u2022The pride of the Fianna (Stag\u2019s Antlers) and their love of life also plays a role in why this tribe in particular has historically been associated with the composition of legends, songs, and master-crafts<br /> \u2022Fianna also embody and highlight another Garou tendency, namely to have relations with spiritual beings; for the Fianna this is highlighted by their regular, ritual, and passionate communions with earthy wild spirits and their Fae associates (and with Stag\u2019s pride in particular this also means that they must boastfully represent their Fae ancestry)<br /> \u2022The Fianna are a tribe where ritual customs such as sleeping with ritual horses or going on quests to enter mystical sexual relations to insure fertility and bounty for the people are represented <br /> <br /> <b>Fenrir </b><br /> \u2022Compare/contrast with the Fianna<br /> \u2022I view the Fenrir as embodying the archetypal form of the \u2018Koryos\u2019 more than any other tribe; a band of warriors who have left the customs of regular and fruitful society, leaving behind the life camps/peace camps of their people, to join together in semi-nomadic war camps <br /> \u2022The Fenrir kinfolk are left to largely regulate themselves with semi-regular check ins or old wolves who are established enough to settle down outside the war-bands but not old enough or weak enough to be voluntarily (or involuntarily) euthanized <br /> \u2022The Fenrir are dedicated to the principles of War-Wolf and Death-Wolf; warriors who consecrate themselves in a willingness to kill and an acceptance of their own death in order to be fearless in battle and to terrorize their enemies and foes<br /> \u2022While the Fenrir are known for their fearless direct battles they have no scruples launching midnight raids on their enemies with silent claws or with whirling noise makers; regardless the Fenrir are the tribe which most embody the archetype of the psychedelic chewing killers who desensitize themselves from fear-of-death through dissociating from self and the glorification of valor (sometimes this valor is what one imagines, the glory of direct battle, but it can also include midnight terror raids and silent killing)<br /> \u2022The Fenrir are led by the most capable, fearless, and brutal of their elders who also take up the role of ritual-doctors for the lower warriors who are brought into the war band<br /> \u2022The Fenrir are far less associated with the Scandinavian aesir gods and far more with the wilderness-mystic gods of the Vanir, wilderness spirits, and giants embodying natural chaos<br /> -(TBH\u2026 under this view I think certain manifestations of Odin actually fit rather well amongst the Fenrir; less the God\u2019s manifestations as a law-keeper and enemy of primordial chaos but more in his roles as a one-eyed cthonic death-warrior god of the wild hunt)<br /> <br /> <b>Glass Walkers</b><br /> \u2022The tribe of Cockroach has certain similarities to Bone Gnawers (who live amongst the developed wreckages - in Garou terms - of human civilization) and the Children of Gaia (who also want to communicate and develop human society towards Gaian ends) while the Glass Walkers are increasingly concerned with the powerful systems developed by Humanity-Weaver and put to use<br /> \u2022The Glass Walkers are the closest tribe to the study of the Weaver and of humanity in relation and how they and the systems they generate might be useful for the Garou Nation and Mother Gaia (any Garou who uses language or a klaive is participating in the Weaver\u2019s world whether they like it or not, the Glass Walkers embrace that and carry it on to its logical extremes)<br /> \u2022Glass Walkers are the tribe most at risk of falling into the taint of the Weaver; which namely would occur of servicing the systems of the Weaver and developing their power for the sake of that power rather then constraining and putting it to the benefit of the Mother and being able to better sabotage the Weaver\u2019s machinery from within<br /> \u2022The Cockroach is a survivor, an ingenious survivor, which sheds any detritus and flourish for the purpose of better survival; the Glass Walkers have embraced the Weaver and Humanity and have shed their Ancestors and Pure Breed in order to better maneuver the cold engines of the Weaver","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T13:45:46-07:00","id":1514237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1514146#post1514146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always associated the Black Furies with the larger Ancient Greek world, including the Black Sea region (modern Turkey, Ukraine, the Caucasus), Syria, parts of the Balkans, Italy, and the various islands of the eastern Mediterranean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to match the Black Furies to the Greek legends of the Amazons as well. I think it was a mistake for the game to match the Black Furies to the Greeks. The writers clearly wanted to link them to the Amazons, but forgot the Amazons were actually barbarians to the Greeks, not part of the Greeks themselves. I don't mind some connections to the Greeks, because the legends show multiple cases of intermarriage between Greek men and the Amazons, but the majority of the Black Fury kinfolk should match up to where the Greeks located them - primarily (but not exclusively) with the Eurasian steppe (from Ukraine to Central Asia), areas around the Black Sea in the Caucasus and Anatolia, and &quot;Libya&quot; (North Africa).<br /> <br /> I am fine with the Black Fury totem and even using the name &quot;Pegasus&quot; for it. But if I ever wanted to emphasize the difference between the spirit and Greek myth, I'd use the term &quot;white winged horse&quot; instead. <br /> <br /> The color white, like silver, is a lunar color. It connects the spirit to the moon, just like how the Furies say &quot;Artemis&quot; (another Greek term, but for our purposes is just an Incarna of the Celestine Luna that is capable of interacting with the Garou and is known by lots of different names) sent Pegasus. This is a lunar spirit.<br /> <br /> It being winged demonstrates the spirit is a messenger from the celestial heavens - an important intermediary between Luna and the material world. That means the spirit is a divine messenger, bringing the wisdom of the moon to the Garou. And the moon has long been a symbol of the feminine because of the correspondence of the moon's cycle to menstruation. It being winged is extremely important to its function. This all fits with the standard Black Fury narrative as well.<br /> <br /> Lastly, it is a horse spirit. The Furies are said to be one of the oldest tribes - perhaps the second oldest tribe. We see the horse as a domesticated animal now, but back then it was not. In fact, the horse would not be domesticated until quite late compared to other animals, long after the Impergium ended. So at the time, an equine spirit would be seen as something of the Wyld. An untamed and undomesticated animal. The figure of a &quot;white horse&quot; shows up in a lot of mythologies, usually representing a being of exceptional powers, divinity, or excellence. So it would be an appropriate symbolic or real carrier of the power of the sacred feminine from Luna to earth. That power isn't just a representation of the feminine - it is a power that protects and avenges. Wild horses can be incredibly dangerous so it can be an appropriate totem for a tribe of Furies/avengers.<br /> <br /> (Unicorn bears many of these attributes as well, but in this case the color white does not represent a connection to Luna, but as a symbol for purity.)<br /> <br /> As long as we remember &quot;Pegasus&quot; is just an obvious name for the spirit given it's description, and go back to what mythic associations its description would have, we can accept the spirit as something that long predates the Greeks. On the other hand, switching Gorgon for Pegasus doesn't seem to me that it solves any &quot;problems&quot; with the spirit and merely substitutes one cultural specific being for another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T12:18:18-07:00","id":1514330,"title":"","content":"Some more tribal head canons and thoughts\u2026 (Part 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons</b><br /> \u2022Black Fox has a thread about Gryphon as a totem which I think has some great Red Talon ideas; in particular their association with the primeval wilderness, acting as guardians, and relations to leadership <br /> \u2022A counter-part to the Glass Walkers in a similar way that Fianna-Fenrir can be counterparts or that Silver Fangs-Bone Gnawers or Black Furies-Shadow Lords<br /> \u2022Red Talons are a relatively reclusive tribe, mostly found in the last great wild places where great wild packs are able to form <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Lords</b><br /> \u2022The Shadow Lords imo benefit from being as global as the Silver Fangs who they \u2018shadow\u2019 (heh) but like the Silver Fangs they can also have a tribal center in the deep caucasus mountains and/or Siberia<br /> \u2022I view the Shadow Lords as taking on a role of diametric opposition with the Black Furies for reasons that should become more clear below<br /> \u2022Grandfather Thunder, the Shadow Lord spirit patron (totem) is in my opinion a prime fit for being associated with primordial storm-father/storm-warrior archetypes (Zeus, Jupiter, Thor*, Indra, Yahweh, etc.)<br /> \u2022Grandfather Thunder in the distant past probably originated in a pair along the lines of Father Sky-Mother Earth with the pre-eminence placed upon Mother Earth (a form of veneration the Black Furies in particular will fiercely uphold) and over time, in certain places, Father Sky and related manifestations began to take on pre-eminence as Fertilizer &amp; Life-Giver over Mother Earth as part of a father-cult overtaking a mother-cult <br /> \u2022In the WoD we also know that at some point along the process one of the seeds of the Weaver would adopt the form of the Patriarch, a spiritual representation of the father-cult which would emerge from the Storm-Fathers and would form the basis for a Patriarchal Law-Giver Order; an order which the Shadow Lords would recognize the power within and adopt for themselves <br /> \u2022The Shadow Lords would have a role defined by their proximity to power and their role as the stewards of authority and power in spiritual terms (whereas the Silver Fangs would be the ritual-vessels of power); for the Shadow Lords this would mean strictly maintaining the power of the highest authority, crushing dissent, and a willingness to use whatever tactics necessary <br /> \u2022The Shadow Lords and the Black Furies both upheld some of the darkest ritual duties of the father-cult and mother-cults respectively, albeit with different approaches and philosophies. Both of these tribes held the silent knives and night killers who would uphold the respective taboos of one spirit-cult or the other<br /> \u2022The Shadow Lords adopt the role of \u2018villain\u2019 whenever it is necessary for the power of the Silver Fangs and/or the Nation<br /> \u2022The Shadow Lords closely follow the Silver Fangs and are also consumed by their own dedication to power and authority. The Shadow Lords traditionally are the star council which watches the Silver Fangs for any signs of weakness, impurity, impotence, cowardice, or incompetence - should the signs of this be discovered the preparations are made for the Killing of the King rituals; by which the spirit of the Silver Fang is cut off before it can decay and so is passed along to the successor <br /> \u2022A core divide of the Shadow Lords in the modern era as the Silver Fang decline and decay becomes more pronounced is over their role. Some Shadow Lords believe that they must remain to the old role of supporting the Silver Fangs lest they lose themselves to power-madness as the Fangs have. Other believe, either out of genuine interest or self-interest, that the Silver Fangs must be usurped and the legitimacy of the Nation be removed from the Silver Fangs and placed into the body of the Nation itself (which may or may not be headed by a vanguard council of Shadow Lord elders)<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders</b><br /> \u2022I think that the Egyptian plot of the Silent Striders (&amp; Followers of Set and Cult of Isis and Children of Osiris and Horus, etc.) benefits from adding some flairs of Howardian and Lovecraftian eldritch horror and hyperboreanism, also somewhat reminiscent of the NWOD\u2019s Mage or Mummy gamelines<br /> \u2022The Silent Striders are the tribe who maintains the ancient, secret, and eldritch taboos, bindings, and mysteries of the Land of Magick prior to their cataclysmic confrontation with the Cult of Set in the past sands of time<br /> \u2022The Silent Striders, under Owl, are now dedicated to being the silent guardians of dead mysteries and secrets (as well as the mysteries and secrets of the dead); activities such as guarding ancient death scrolls which could unleash elder demons of the Settian cult or tablets which contain fragments of the earliest dictates of the magicians or the last words of the pre-historic god-kings<br /> \u2022The Silent Striders now are dedicated both to the keeping of their ancient mysteries but also in general the acquisition of other knowledges which they can spread amongst their fellow Garou in exchange for brief respites at their hearths and camps<br /> \u2022The Silent Striders are feared, reviled, and pitied by the other tribes; their knowledge and gifts are recognized but they are fundamentally a tribe of Post-Apocalypse and considered as such <br /> \u2022The Silent Striders have a similar niche to Older Brother or the Stargazers; but is made distinct by a greater interest in the dead and of mysteries which are not simply old or dark (like Older Brother) but are truly Dead and of Epochs which no longer exist (and according to mortal historians may never have existed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:17:49-07:00","id":1514385,"title":"","content":"My slightly alternate take on the Gurahl, Gaia's Succor.<br /> <br /> The auspices.<br /> <br /> <b>Spring</b>: Succor as the Healer. They are called to encourage and nurture new growth, as well as recovery from past trauma. This includes mental and spiritual injury as well as physical, and a special emphasis on children. They also work to heal natural sites, communities, and parts of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer</b>: Succor as the Guardian. They are called to defend and protect their charges, and to help them learn to defend themselves. While their focus is often sacred sites, natural areas, and communities, it will also at times involve specific individuals, powerful fetishes, and lost lore.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn</b>: Succor as the Teacher. They are called to instruct and guide those in need, helping them understand and accept their place in Gaia's greater world. Often wise beyond their years, and instinctively able to understand others, many work to encourage their charges and help them grow into their true selves.<br /> <br /> <b>Winter</b>: Succor as the Priest. They are called to tend to the greatest and gravest of spiritual matters, including guiding the sick and dying to peace and helping the spirits of the dead pass over. They council against grief and loss, and help make way for the new growth that is to come.<br /> <br /> And the Lodges, the social groupings which take the place of tribes, and are not really bound by geographic location.<br /> <br /> <i>The Lodge of the Green Earth</i>, nurturers and protectors of growing things, including ecosystems and children.<br /> <i>The Lodge of the Healing Heart</i>, ambassadors and peacemakers devoted to soothing conflicts and building bridges between people and communities.<br /> <i>The Lodge of the Star Mother</i>, devoted to the arts of astrology and prophecy, providing guidance and encouragement to those in need.<br /> <i>The Lodge of the Whispering Winds</i>, mystics and umbra explorers who spend much of their time in the Umbra and healing spirits, including the restless dead of the Dark Umbra.<br /> <i>The Lodge of the Sleeping Kings</i>, historians and protectors of sacred places, including the lairs of ancient Gurahl elders who have been slumbering for centuries and millennia.<br /> <i>The Lodge of the Cave Bear</i>, an all-ursine sect fiercely devoted to protecting nature and their kinfolk from humans and other forces. (They are the most likely to have secret ties with the Red Talons.)<br /> <br /> In addition, there are a few regional groups that are more culturally oriented rather than involving specific mechanics or foci.<br /> <br /> The <i>Jambavana</i> are the Gurahl of the Indian subcontinent. Among the local changing breeds, they are usually seen as being akin to the Brahmin caste (alongside the Makara and the local Stargazers and Children of Gaia), and are skilled demon fighters.<br /> The <i>Okami</i> are the Gurahl of Korea, Japan, Manchuria, and parts of China. They are often part of the Beast Courts of the Emerald Mother. (Not extinct.)<br /> The <i>Artio</i> are - or were - the Gurahl of the European subcontinent, but were mostly destroyed by the Garou during the various Wars of Rage. Only a handful still exist, doing everything they can to stay hidden. Many are part of the Lodge of Sleeping Kings.<br /> The <i>Otso</i> are the Gurahl of Fennoscandia and northwest Russia. While decimated similarly to the Artio, they have slowly recovered to a better degree, mostly owing to pure stubborn determination.\u200b<br /> The <i>Goah</i> are the native Gurahl of the Eastern Woodlands and Great Lakes. In the days of the Pure Lands, they were the ones with the closest ties to the Three Brothers and other breeds. (There are different groups in the Southwest, Pacific Northwest, and other regions.)<br /> The <i>Nanook</i> are the native Gurahl of North America's Arctic regions, mainly of polar bear stock. Powerful hunters, they are also strict enforcers of spiritual taboos.<br /> \u200bThe <i>Nandi</i> are rumored to be Gurahl native to East Africa, but no one has actually seen one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:08:43-07:00","id":1514508,"title":"","content":"Lots of Head-Canon but here\u2019s some main areas:<br /> <br /> The War of Rage wasn\u2019t just the Garou waging war on other shifters, it was the end of the Mythic Age, the separation of Gaias realm and the gauntlet was the actual reason for most of the shifter extinction due to the violent separation of worlds.<br /> <br /> The atrocities of the WOR was inflicted by the Garou, Bastet and Mokole.<br /> <br /> A number of prey animal shifters (moles, rodents) survived but did so through hiding in the Inner Earths, with the help of the spirit realms.<br /> <br /> There are Owl Shifters (not the SV version) originating from Europe.<br /> <br /> There are remnants of other Garou tribes alongside the main tribes, The Bardor in England etc, most dwell within larger tribes like the Fianna but they retain their own totems and gifts.<br /> <br /> The only lost tribe that is truly extinct is the Croatian as they sacrificed their souls to defeat the Eater of Souls, there is the potential for White Howlers and Bunypi to be born from pure blood kinfolk.<br /> <br /> The Fianna are much more involved with the Fey with Rites connecting to Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T18:24:40-07:00","id":1514532,"title":"","content":"Some of my Head-Canon:<br /> -No Golgol Fang-First, the war in the Amazon is fought by native shapeshifters from Brazil, Peru, Colombia, Equador, Bolivia, Venezuela, Suriname, Guiana, and French Guiana;<br /> <br /> -The Hengeyokai e Kue jin has a strong presence in Brazil, since thanks the japanese imigration, Brasil has the largest Japanese population outside Japan;<br /> <br /> -Hengeyokai court organization has influenced the native shapeshifters (Garou included) an d<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"color:#252525\">gave rise to the Nagual Council, bringing together the members</span></span></span>\u200bgarou, mokol\u00e9, bastet, ratkin and corax;<br /> <br /> -Vampires are all result of Vicissitude been a disease of the Eater of Souls (yep, that version of Vicissitude, I like this), no Camarilla, no Sabath, no dance macabre. There is older vampires,but they are more like the Master from Strain trilogy;<br /> <br /> -The Maeljin Incarna and the Yomi Kings are the same entities, diferent names just that...<br /> <br /> -Grandmother is a head of Wyrm;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:21:02-07:00","id":1514606,"title":"","content":"Some more tribal head-canons and thoughts\u2026 (Part 4)<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs</b><br /> \u2022The Silver Fangs are diametrically opposite with the Bone Gnawers <br /> \u2022The Silver Fangs represent the archetype of the sacred-king/queen; physical vessels for a quasi-divine potency of spirit which embodies the people, their relationship with the spiritual, and a physical vessel for the world<br /> \u2022Powerful Silver Fang kings/queen with the proper rituals will reflect their mental and physical state in the land itself; where the Gauntlet is high this may be limited to the Sept but legend says that the Silver Fangs of old would cause storms with their anger or abundant fertility with their good humor <br /> \u2022The ur-place of any Silver Fang is as King/Queen but naturally not all can fill such roles; as such other Silver Fangs will either settle into auxiliary roles (Champions, Rite-Keepers, Inquisitors, etc.) but in particular the classic Garou ideal of a non-King/Queen Silver Fang is as the heroic alpha of a Garou pack leading them on great adventures and exploits<br /> \u2022The Silver Fangs have become broken as the ages have gone on and the reasons/explanations for this vary: some say that the bloodlines have become polluted and must be purified, others say that liberal/lac enforcement of the high customs (including the Killing of the King\u2026) have allowed inner rot, others say that the Silver Fangs are suffering power-madness from overstepping the original taboos they had won from Sun and Moon in exchange for authority, others say the Silver Fangs embody the corruption of the world and that the pollution of the land itself has riddled their minds, others say that the curse of Father Wolf has struck the tribe or they have disappointed Falcon, others say it is because of a lack of new young Silver Fangs being sired or worthy of Falcon; regardless of the cause what everyone can agree on is that the average Silver Fang is slowly dissolving into a matrix of neuroses and aberrations which undermine their competency <br /> \u2022Legends vary as to how the Silver Fangs gained their authority; the tribe itself guards closely held secrets about communion with White Wolf (Death) itself, while variations of the stories of primordial Silver Fangs winning the blessing of Sun and thus the power of sacred kingship also remain (some Black Furies suspect that it\u2019s the solar power of Sun itself which has caused the madness by its conjunction with the lunar power of Moon that was meant to be the Garou birth rite)<br /> \u2022Silver Fangs are a global tribe and the guardians of the most ancient, sacred, and powerful artifacts and places; making their gradual degeneration all the more worrying<br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers</b><br /> \u2022The Stargazers are not the only tribe of Asia, but that\u2019s a whole larger conversation; in particular the Stargazers are renowned for keeping mountain top septs close to the heavens, which is why they\u2019re particularly associated with the powerful Caern of the High Himalayas<br /> \u2022The Stargazers are a rather esoteric and unusual tribe due to the Auspices of Chimera; the star-beast and the dream-creature, because of Chimera the Stargazers are drawn to contemplating the mysteries of heaven, mind, and spirit<br /> \u2022Stargazers more than any other tribe (with honorable mention given to the Silent Striders and Older Brother) are renowned for their private hermitages and trials to discover spiritual and philosophical secrets and to explore powerful Mysteries (including things which would not be out of place for a Mage chronicle)<br /> \u2022The Stargazers are a relatively small tribe who often disappear into the Umbra or into remote places of contemplation; at their best they are the philosophical pioneers of what is possible for the Nation but at their worst they are entirely absent due to their incessant navel-gazing<br /> <br /> <b>Older Brother (Ghost Council/Whispering Shades)</b><br /> \u2022The spirit patron of the tribe is the Horned Serpent<br /> \u2022Older Brother is associated with water and cthonic mysteries amongst the tribes of the Americas; in particular OB has always been associated with taboos, secrets, esoteric societies, mysteries, subtlety, and cunning; being renowned in the modern nights for creating some of the most gifted Theurges in the world<br /> \u2022Older Brother has adopted the policies of assimilation, adaption, and horizontal adoptionism as its means for surviving the Post-Apocalypse <br /> \u2022Older Brother, more than any other tribe, engages in the practice of poaching secrets and practices from non-Garou sorcerers<br /> \u2022Older Brother is also renowned for their capacity to engage in work with dark spirits, even the Old Wyrm Spirits, with more skill and care than any other tribe; at their best this makes them unparalleled as theurges and the best at understanding the Wyrm but at their worst they know better than any tribe the dangers of the Wyrm and its pollution <br /> <br /> <b>Younger Brother (Gale Stalkers)</b><br /> \u2022The spirit patron of the tribe is the Great Fisher (although I must admit I do have a soft-spot for the notion of giving YB Hairy-Man/Sasquatch as their tribal patron; something about the liminal space between human life and the non-human natural world seems fitting to me)<br /> \u2022Younger Brother is associated with air and vital motion amongst the native tribes of the Americas (with water and cthonic mysteries being Older Brother and earth and rock solidity being Middle Brother)<br /> \u2022Younger Brother has adopted a policy of Survival, Resistance, and Militancy to the Post-Apocalypse both on martial, material, and social terms<br /> \u2022Younger Brother is more closely associated with the pre-Apocalyptic rites, customs, and mysteries then perhaps any other tribe; embodying the persistence of those consequences into the modern nights and carrying out the ancient duties and associations in order to keep their sacred wheels turning","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:55:26-07:00","id":1514753,"title":"","content":"Something that I think would be an interesting addition to werewolf and could be useful within its milleau is a greater attention paid to cults.<br /> <br /> For one, if we really get down to it Pentex, one of the central antagonists of the setting, is essentially a vast and extremely resourceful cult. In my opinion PENTEX also really pops in the places where they combine the banal horror of just what a profit-seeking corporation does on its own terms with the occasional conscious ventures into actual witchcraft and black magic to spread taint (I\u2019m thinking things like the witch episodes of the X-Files, the law firm from \u2018Angel\u2019, the group from \u2018Rosemary\u2019s Baby\u2019, etc.). The idea that not only is, for instance, this schlock GI Joe knockoff action figure a tool of social education and made from shitty plastic and paint, but that it also has a dark voodoo style curse placed on it which will effect its user. I think that\u2019s a rich field of material to work with.<br /> <br /> I like to add more cult type groups to the setting in general. For instance most Halloween style witch covens or horror movie satanic cults are great fits for Wyrm style cults you can have in your game. I also think that there\u2019s interesting things you can do for other spirit groups. For the Wyld I\u2019d imagine taking inspiration from irl Situationist &amp; Discordian Groups (which I think old White Wolf writers also did on occasion, iirc there are even a couple books that have the sign off of \u2018Hail Eris!\u2019 in them) - I\u2019d imagine a combination of pure LSD/Hippie style shock-freak sufis to more high flown mind-fuck style groups with Hail Bob or Ong\u2019s Hat ARG vibes; creating memetic viruses to infect and alter reality. Furthermore while I think most actual religions can be used as inspiration for Weaver cults given the Weaver, I always get drawn towards two other molds: one is the faux psychiatric mold which has Weaver cults which are basically Scientology with the serial numbers filed off or Weaver Cults that are basically cells of a Masonic Bavarian Illuminati style org. I also think that one could take inspiration from something like Alan Moore\u2019s work or WtF to have more miscellaneous cults.<br /> <br /> Ultimately however the issue I run up onto is how to scale this for Werewolf in particular. For instance having Alan Moore/Hellblazer style groups running around the WoD is fitting for the setting I think, but how do you tailor it for different games. I can see the average cult being able to provide a mystery and intrigue plot line for a werewolf game but when it comes to action it feels like in most cases it\u2019s a walk in the park for the Garou. I suppose what I can suggest for that then is that the Garou mostly deal with successful cults that have made contact with powerful spirits and fomori/monsters who can challenge the Garou physically or one uses cults as one tool in the box for their game - that in the same way you have straight-forward punch-em-ups with monstrous fomori (but without much need for investigation or intrigue) you can have investigation and intrigue challenges based around cults that, once they\u2019ve unwound the mystery, you let your players have a power trip of dishing out whatever horror movie scenario they cook up to deal with these doomed cultists.<br /> <br /> Anyway these are just a few thoughts I had on the topic, I\u2019d be curious to hear any thoughts other people had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:11:36-07:00","id":1514757,"title":"","content":"I had meant to get around to talking about cults in my ridiculously oversized Pentex thread, but a bunch of stuff happened, and I kept forgetting to update it. \ud83d\ude1e<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:54:52-07:00","id":1514764,"title":"","content":"Excited to see any material you\u2019ve got when it\u2019s ready to be shown! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T12:43:46-07:00","id":1515173,"title":"","content":"<b>Headcanon and Homebrews</b><br /> So as it\u2019s in the same Imperium Victorian worldline/setting in 1869 as Mage although our Werewolf games are in the Savage West.<br /> <br /> The Garou can gain small mystic knacks that can individualise their gifts.<br /> <br /> The Storm Eater is free but hasn\u2019t consuming a weaver Incarna yet, however it\u2019s consumption of smaller weaver spirits is breaking the pattern web.<br /> <br /> A number of factors exist at an earlier stage for example the Umbral Pilots are Victorian pioneers.<br /> <br /> Wandering mixed packs are relatively common although Septs are pretty suspicious to each other, inter tribal conflict is frequent and viscous between the Pure Ones and Wyrm Comers Midwest to the west coast.<br /> <br /> The Older and Younger Brothers are aligned with the Nunnehi, they often share totems and work together to defend Caern/Glades.<br /> <br /> The Hungry Dead have attempted to invade San Francisco whilst the State is relatively new and unclaimed, the younger Wan Rai seek to even the loss of territory in the orient to imperial invaders or to escape the Taipan Civil War.<br /> <br /> The Garou have secured a number of power sites (fonts, Dragon Nests and a few full caerns, the Golden Bay has many) which has brought them into conflict with the Hungry Dead.<br /> <br /> In reaction to the Storm Eater the Rokea have started to actively guard the waters of the West Coast sinking ships carrying supernatural passengers, including some technocratic vessels.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-15-2023, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T15:11:46-07:00","id":1515184,"title":"","content":"PENTEX: The Founding Pentarchy<br /> <br /> Today a multi-billion dollar international holding company, Pentex was founded in 1915 as <i>Five Corners Holdings</i>, a financial consolidation of five preexisting companies. They gradually continued to expand, absorbing more and more companies over the decades. The holding company became <i>Pentex Investments</i> in the 1940s, and finally just Pentex in the 1980s. While some of Pentex's holdings are openly traded on the stock markets, Pentex itself is a private company, largely unknown to the general public or even much of the modern press. Pentex prefers it this way, and people who unknowingly start digging into their operations tend to meet bad ends.<br /> Each of the founding companies was in service to a different powerful Wyrm entity or faction, and because of this backing, combined with their role as founders, each is a powerful block within the greater hydra that is Pentex.<br /> <br /> <b>Endron Energy International</b><br /> Founded in Pennsylvania as <i>Premium Oil</i> after the American Civil War, it moved to Texas a decade later. While drilling there, company head Jeremiah Lassiter unleashed an ancient Wyrm entity, one so old even the Three Brothers knew of it only from the most ancient of lore. The being, dating back to the time of the Mokole and the Dinosaur Kings, is known only as <i>Black Blood of the Earth</i>. It tried to dominate Lassiter, but his will proved too strong to outright control, and instead they struck a pact, offering power in exchange for influence in the modern world. The strain of resisting the entity's power eventually proved too much for Lassiter, leading to his death from cancer and mental strain.<br /> Today, Endron is a global leader in energy technology, extraction, production, and distribution. While petroleum has long been the backbone of their company, they have continued to expand into the areas of nuclear power (absorbing the Atlas Energy Company in the 1980s), hydroelectric, and now solar and wind power. While their recent interest in renewables would seem to run counter to the overall goals of Pentex and the Wyrm, the massive quantities of rare earths and other metals (often strip mined in other countries), the impact of wind farms on avian and sea life, the unreliability of renewables, the corruption of government subsidies to &quot;green&quot; energy, and the coming flood of un-recyclable solar panel and wind turbine parts are all part of a long game.<br /> <br /> <b>HH Mineral Resources</b><br /> Originally <i>Harold Brothers' Mining Company</i>, founded in the Ohio River Valley near the start of the 19th century to extract coal, iron and other materials for America's burgeoning industry. During the 1830s, a mysterious artifact was found in a mine in what is now West Virginia. The relic of a prehistoric - perhaps even prehuman - civilization, made of an unknown material and inscribed with a single untranslatable glyph, it soon drove both company founders violently mad. One brother killed the other, and created a cult devoted to the artifact. Originally consisting of the Harold brothers' families, and later the inner circle of the company's leadership, the cult has slowly tickled down into the populous of certain mining towns. The being it referred to only by a single syllable bark/cough-like noise that causes pain to the uninitiated.<br /> HH Mineral Resources is a global powerhouse in mining and mineral extraction, operating on six continents (and if they could, they'd be strip mining Antarctica). Iron and other metals, coal, rare earths, salt, silicone, uranium, diamonds, and asbestos are all part of their portfolio. Deep tunnel mining (including into lost and labyrinthine caverns within the earth), strip mining, and chemical leaching leave massive damage to the environment, while frequent use of child and even slave labor leave spiritual scars.<br /> The company has one of the longest standing relationships with the Black Spiral Dancers, with some tribe members and their kinfolk having joined the nameless cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Smith &amp; Young Company/SYC</b><br /> Founded in Indiana in the 1850s as a soap and candle manufacturer, it has always been a front for the <i>Red Circle</i>, a secretive cult of Wyrm witches dating back to medieval times (and perhaps the Roman Empire). Their marketing and logos include subtle markings and symbols of their cult and the Wyrm. Membership in the Circle is a requirement to be part of the board or even many upper management positions. Toward that end, they have a number of recruitment arms among college Greek organizations and internship programs.<br /> SYC currently manufactures and sells over a hundred different brands, including personal hygiene, cleaning supplies, cosmetics, chewing gum, snack foods, cooking oils, ice cream, family planning, baby supplies, diet and health products, tea, coffee, and condiments. They are almost ubiquitous in the Western world, especially North America. Individually, their products are often harmless, contributing to Pentex's aims primarily through packaging and other waste. However, their packaging and logos can attract the attention of Banes and other spirits, and certain combinations of products may result in unexpected and freakish results.<br /> <br /> <b>Alegro Global</b><br /> Perhaps one of the oldest of all Pentex companies, originating in colonial Virginia as <i>Clayton Tobacco</i>. By the start of the 20th century, the <i>Clayton Brands Tobacco Company</i> was a major grower and provider of tobacco and tobacco products in the United States and Canada. With the public backlash against tobacco companies in the 1990s and early 2000s, Clayton changed their name to Alegro Global, but continue their same business. Since its founding, the company has always been under the influence of <i>Lord Choke</i>, the Elemental Maeljin of Smoke and Smog. This, combined with their enormous profits from the Asian markets, allow them to maintain their place of power within Pentex.<br /> Alegro markets a wide range of products under various labels, including cigarettes of various price points meant to cater to different economic brackets. (They pride themselves on being one of the companies to initially promote smoking as acceptable to women.) In addition, they offer various smokeless tobaccos such as dip and snuff, pipe tobacco, and cigars. Their brands have long been major sponsors of various motorsports around the globe, and membership rewards programs have long offered customers the chance to send in proofs of purchase for all manner of company branded merchandise (including various mascots that were appealing to teenagers). Their tobacco has long been modified with chemicals and other methods to increase its nicotine output and addictiveness. Lately, the rise of e-cigarettes and vaping threatened to cut into their market shares, but their promotion of anti-vaping legislation has given them time to start developing their own vaping products.<br /> <br /> <b>Logan Foods Corporation </b><br /> Founded in Chicago during the civil war to sell rotted canned meat (often from horses) to the Union armies, <i>Logan Meat Packing Company</i> used various political and criminal connections to become one of the America's major meat suppliers. They controlled every part of their operation from stockyards to slaughterhouses to butchers to salesmen. The founder, Garfield Logan, was in fact a cannibal and murderer who worshiped a Wyrm entity he called <i>&quot;The God of Meat&quot;</i>, but which The Three Brothers knew as <i>That Which Devours All Flesh</i>. The leadership of the company still worships this spirit, holding annual corporate retreats that involve hunting and grilling. Usually of people.<br /> Currently the company is one of the world's largest processors and marketers of beef, pork, and poultry. Certain sub brands also specialize in various exotic meats, as well as (allegedly), free range, organic, kosher, and halal offerings, as well as various frozen foods, pet foods, and jerkies. Many of the animals used by Logan's are pumped full of growth hormones, including experimental ones being tested for Pentex super-soldier programs, and frequently housed in less-than-ideal conditions. Over the decades, their plants have caused massive levels of water pollution, especially among poorer areas of Southern states. (State governments would frequently look the other way in exchange for campaign contributions or offering corporate positions to family members.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 06-15-2023, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T00:09:53-07:00","id":1515212,"title":"","content":"I have many issues with the depiction of PENTEX in Werewolf, and I feel it has gotten worse with each new edition. I think many writers just don't understand basic corporate structure. At least you have gotten it right - PENTEX as some kind of investment firm with its various companies being their own thing. Many writers seem to think it is actually just a single large conglomerate, and don't realize that the &quot;Directors&quot; should be board of directors and that is different from management.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I do have a PENTEX conspiracy that is based more from the movie <i>They Live</i> than WoD sourcebooks, and some of the &quot;subsidiaries&quot; split off into their own separate, unrelated Wyrm cults. And I think some of the companies just are not gameable at the table and thus useless to the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1515184#post1515184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the 1830s, a mysterious artifact was found in a mine in what is now West Virginia. The relic of a prehistoric - perhaps even prehuman - civilization, made of an unknown material and inscribed with a single untranslatable glyph, it soon drove both company founders violently mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this angle. It could easily be tied to the Vhujunka, which in my chronicles are often analogous to the Serpent People of Robert E. Howard and Clark Ashton Smith. Or since it is from North America, it might be related to the Gamor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:49:46-07:00","id":1515306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1515212#post1515212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this angle. It could easily be tied to the Vhujunka, which in my chronicles are often analogous to the Serpent People of Robert E. Howard and Clark Ashton Smith. Or since it is from North America, it might be related to the Gamor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess that I largely borrowed the idea from Stephen King's novel Desperation, as well as one of the plot threads from Dragon Age 2. <br /> <br /> They Live is good Pentex viewing. \ud83d\udc4d<br /> <br /> I wish I could remember who said it (around 20 years ago), to the effect that a lot of early Pentex material was clearly written by people who hated corporate America but even more clearly had no idea how any of it really worked. That was part of why I started my Pentex thread several years ago, and also why I tried to include a lot of books that talked about how each industry actually functions, as well as its history and evolution. (Endron today is going to be a somewhat different beast today than it was back in the 70s, for example.) Also why some of the last few entries I did were about corporate culture and basic economics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T12:59:21-07:00","id":1515551,"title":"","content":"<b>The Pentax Precursor </b><br /> The Southern Ocean Trading Company, founded in 1711 a fake investment house that almost bankrupted the entire British Government in 1720, infamously known as the South Sea Bubble.<br /> <br /> Purchased in 1829 by the mysterious McGrath family, hailing from Scotland they migrated to Liverpool (or Liuerpul) during the time of Edward Longshanks, the Hammer of the Scots\u200b (by betraying their clansmen an act that incurred the emnity of the Dursirn Clan).<br /> <br /> A family of Wyrm cultists many of their children pure-blood Ferectoi\u200b, the company registered in London and Hudson Bay has interests in logging, shipping, the fur trade, whaling, fishing, merchant goods and retail.<br /> <br /> Having encountered heavy resistance in the Hudson Bay, from surprising incorruptible mortals they have turned their attentions to the boom town of San Francisco and it\u2019s multiple places of power.<br /> <br /> How they fare against the assembled forces of the Kindred, Hungry Dead, Garou and Changelings all contesting the Golden Bay within the Ring of Fire remains to be seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-21-2023, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T17:14:10-07:00","id":1516289,"title":"","content":"Something I've been fiddling with for the Ananasi, still a work in progress.<br /> <br /> Skeins, regional collectives of were-spiders who tend to share similarities in culture, world-view, activities, and Triat orientation. None of them are all encompassing, and numerous Ananasi in those regions aren't part of the dominant Skein. And the nature of modern globalism means that members can often be found all around the globe. <br /> <br /> <i>The Arachne </i>(Eastern Mediterranean and Black Sea) - Primarily oriented toward the Weaver, they are famed as weavers and artisans, as well as traders and merchants, often amassing large amounts of covert political power in various countries. <br /> <br /> <i>Tsuchigumo/Yatsukahagi</i> (Japan) - Primarily oriented toward the Wyrm/Ebon Dragon, they are on the fringes of the Beast Courts, neither enemy nor ally. They are primarily known as thieves, con artists, infiltrators, and assassins. <br /> <br /> <i>The Anansi </i>(West Africa and the Caribbean) - Primarily oriented toward the Wyld. Tricksters, troublemakers, and revolutionaries as well as artists, storytellers, and mystics. <br /> <br /> I'm still poking at some more, including the Cob (Britain), the Maya (India), as well as looking for ideas for the Americas, Australia, and China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T18:33:59-07:00","id":1516293,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Ananasi, a thought I\u2019ve had, is that it might be interesting to have a few quasi-insect changing breeds or fomori sticking around to give them trouble, sort of hold-overs from the Insect Wars. I\u2019m not particularly fond of the crawling ones but it feels like it would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> For example I imagine that you could have Weaver-aligned Ants, Wyrm-aligned Maggots &amp; Wyrms, Wyld-aligned Larvae &amp; Butterflies/Moths and perhaps some Gaian Bees to go along (or they could also be Weaver aligned). Basically the idea would be, like how the Rokea are implied to have particular undersea splats that they tangle with, so should the Ananasi have their own creepy crawling setting that they tangle with to carry out their missions on behalf of the Spider Queen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T18:59:44-07:00","id":1516298,"title":"","content":"I have used something similar to Forsaken's Hosts as the remains of the insect beings the Ananasi warred with. Mainly wasps, ants, locusts, and roaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T19:56:48-07:00","id":1516305,"title":"","content":"The Hosts in general are something which I think that WtA could crib to some use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T23:06:05-07:00","id":1516319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1516298#post1516298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have used something similar to Forsaken's Hosts as the remains of the insect beings the Ananasi warred with. Mainly wasps, ants, locusts, and roaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s scratched an itch, I was pondering on some form of remnant of the insect changers.<br /> <br /> Like the idea of being non-Wyrm (not formori), I like there to be more threats from the umbra than just A,B,C, probably more Gaia, Weaver, Wyld monsters.<br /> <br /> The spirit shard power works well in that even the Ananasi would struggle to kill one, a side war where they are hunted by vengeful insect hosts has great potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-27-2023, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T23:17:08-07:00","id":1516320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1516293#post1516293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically the idea would be, like how the Rokea are implied to have particular undersea splats that they tangle with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting was there any clues to what the Rokea were tangling with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T16:17:27-07:00","id":1516373,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve read the Rokea breed book but iirc there\u2019s some information in there about how the sharks interpret stuff like the triat and it includes things like Wyrm-Krakens and stuff that the weresharks deal with alongside stuff like oil rigs and fishing boats and that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:45:23-07:00","id":1516389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1516373#post1516373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s been a while since I\u2019ve read the Rokea breed book but iirc there\u2019s some information in there about how the sharks interpret stuff like the triat and it includes things like Wyrm-Krakens and stuff that the weresharks deal with alongside stuff like oil rigs and fishing boats and that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do without it; most of the information on Chulorviah and related concepts is in Blood-Dimmed Tides and the W20 Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T10:45:54-07:00","id":1518434,"title":"","content":"sorry if i am breaking any rules, but heres some of my homebrew/headcanon stuff<br /> <br /> Certain famous Black Spiral Dancers, those that did great blows to the Gaian cause, might be risen to the rank of Incarna. Number Two and Hakaken are examples in canon.<br /> <br /> For dooming the Bunyip, Mara the Scream was ascended to the status of Wyrmish Incarna. She is a Bane Totem of Cunning.<br /> <br /> The Xibalbans all talked like Mr. Pages from Fallen London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":". 07-21-2023, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T15:59:15-07:00","id":1518457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518434#post1518434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sorry if i am breaking any rules, but heres some of my homebrew/headcanon stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not breaking any rules, posting your ideas is what\u2019s great about this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518434#post1518434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Xibalbans all talked like Mr. Pages from Fallen London.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn\u2019t across Fallen London before, it would make a great Realm or Hidden Earth, thanks for the inspiration \ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T17:03:29-07:00","id":1518462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518457#post1518457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not breaking any rules, posting your ideas is what\u2019s great about this thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I hadn\u2019t across Fallen London before, it would make a great Realm or Hidden Earth, thanks for the inspiration \ud83d\ude42</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, and you are welcome.<br /> <br /> here are more of my homebrews/headcanons<br /> <br /> the Wyrm as it is known today, the traitic wyrm, the urge wyrms, and the elemental wyrms, are not the true Balancer Wyrm. The true Wyrm lies dormant in the Weavers web, horrorfied by the Hydra it created and went into topor so as to endure the pain and ensure that its trashing would not cause further harm. The Hydra and those who serve it do not want to free the real Wyrm, as it would destroy them on principle. No, they want to loosen the chains holding the Hydra back from rampaging.<br /> <br /> As long as there has been the concept of Economics, there has been orginizations like Pentex. Rich and Powerful humans selling there souls to the Wyrm, poisioning the earth and being the bane of the Garou. Pentex is merely the latest and most successful of these orginizations, and the one most likely to succeed in the Omega Plan, which all of these organizations have had in some form.<br /> <br /> The Mockery Breeds are not original creations of Pentex, for the Wyrm can not truely create. Instead, they are corruptions of long lost breeds, for that is what the Wyrm does, it corrupts. It is only a matter of time before Neuro-Dynamic Labratories begins to churn out Minotaurs (Mockeries of the noble Apis), Hog Walkers (Mockeries of the Grondr), Bloodlicks (Mockeries of the Camazotz), Saber Maws (Mockeries of the Khara) and, once they get there hands on the work of Cernonous, Hollow Walkers (Mockeries of the Bunyip).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:23:56-07:00","id":1518497,"title":"","content":"I had an idea of the mockery breeds of samsa and yeren as new changing breeds created by gaia. The yeren representing an attempt to engage in social control of humans and Samsa representing an absolute last ditch in case of a mass extinction event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T09:47:27-07:00","id":1518539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518462#post1518462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm as it is known today, the traitic wyrm, the urge wyrms, and the elemental wyrms, are not the true Balancer Wyrm. The true Wyrm lies dormant in the Weavers web, horrorfied by the Hydra it created and went into topor so as to endure the pain and ensure that its trashing would not cause further harm. The Hydra and those who serve it do not want to free the real Wyrm, as it would destroy them on principle. No, they want to loosen the chains holding the Hydra back from rampaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I'd always pictured the big three as being multi-dimensional beings anyway, after all they are an order of scale vaster than the greatest Celestine, so the main Wyrm was fragmented by its capture by the Weaver.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the fragment of balance being forced into torpor/hibernation as that explains how there are Balance Wyrm spirits still around and surviving, an interesting through is how the Hydras children react to Balance Wyrm spirits, do they automatically attack them, don't see them, try and corrupt them or give them a wide berth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518462#post1518462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mockery Breeds are not original creations of Pentex, for the Wyrm can not truely create. Instead, they are corruptions of long lost breeds, for that is what the Wyrm does, it corrupts. It is only a matter of time before Neuro-Dynamic Labratories begins to churn out Minotaurs (Mockeries of the noble Apis), Hog Walkers (Mockeries of the Grondr), Bloodlicks (Mockeries of the Camazotz), Saber Maws (Mockeries of the Khara) and, once they get there hands on the work of Cernonous, Hollow Walkers (Mockeries of the Bunyip).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I'd always pictured this as you describe more of a Jurassic Park activity where Wyrm forces have been scouring the Earth and realms for remnants of the fallen changers, using corrupt rituals and science to bring them back as twisted forms.<br /> <br /> Creates some great campaign ideas where theres a race to prevent some faction from uncovering a lost remnant to ressurect in a perverse way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518497#post1518497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea of the mockery breeds of samsa and yeren as new changing breeds created by gaia. The yeren representing an attempt to engage in social control of humans and Samsa representing an absolute last ditch in case of a mass extinction event.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> One fo the SV books for Mockery Breeds has Yeti as uncorrupted Yeren which I really like, the idea of Gaia trying to create a shifter from an animal relative of man is really good.<br /> <br /> For the Samsa I go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> 's idea of using the WTF Hosts for insect changers returning to prey on humanity and hunt the Ananasi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 07-22-2023, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T11:26:32-07:00","id":1518545,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27824_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27824\" data-vbnamecard=\"27824\">Arcanus</a> <br /> <br /> I picture them trying to corrupt surviving balance spirits, and if that fails they try to destroy them. <br /> <br /> Yes, i live your idea on the jurassic park mockeries/race to prevent new mockery breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:20:28-07:00","id":1518555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1518545#post1518545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, i live your idea on the jurassic park mockeries/race to prevent new mockery breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>My head-canon is that the Glasswalkers survived for several reasons, they could hide more effectively amongst mankind and within cities but also because a couple of tribes recognised their usefulness those being the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> Both have interests in human institutions, both have a healthy distrust of vampires and both have a vested interest in slowing the spread of Pentax.<br /> <br /> The GW might make the SFs and SLs uncomfortable but they are too useful not to have around, so both tribes veto or sabotage attempts by the more primal tribes to outright attack the GWs (I can see them being more willing to sacrifice the Red Talons than GW).<br /> <br /> I\u2019d go as far as saying the GWs could be the reason why the Fangs have held onto power in some locales, secret behind closed door alliances where they protect each others interests.<br /> <br /> The GWs would be the perfect tribe to spot the Mockeries first, definitely the Yeren but also others, their pattern spider spies would be looking out for odd activities particularly ones that link business activities with curious umbral activities.<br /> <br /> So a good conspiracy game could be the GWs investigating the activities of a conservation group that is conducting odd acquisitions in the material world whilst at the same time there appear to be equally unusual activities in the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T13:20:49-07:00","id":1518841,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">more homebrews and headcanons</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">More on Mockery Breeds (if you want to use the ones I create, please ask me first)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mockery Breeds can only be made from the dna of Gaian shifters who are dead, or are very close to dying out.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The War Wolves are made using DNA from the various dead/dying Garou breeds, such as the half eaten remenants of the Croatoan and the Singing Dogs (who might as well be dead, given there are four left).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The hollow walkers, once they become a true mockery breed, will be a source of tension between the Black Spiral Dancers and Pentex. The dancers consider the Hollow Walkers theres, as the first pack and there creator walked the spiral. However, Pentex argues that Bunyip were different enough to nullify the argument. Enterprising Garou could use this to sow dissent in the Wyrms ranks.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Apis come the Minotaurs, who are obsessed with mazes and used by Pentex as guards for various things. The influence of the Minotaur totem upon them is a cause for concern among Pentex management. They completely lack any gifts and magics that the Apis used as Gaias matchmakers, though they are very lusty.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Camazotz come the Bloodlicks, beasts of bat and human merged together. They were an attempt at making sneaky spies, but they quickly proved uncontrollable as there bloodlust was insatiable and the death screams of the Camazotz and the rage of the Bat Bane totem and the attempts of the Gaian Bat Totem to redeem them makes them utterly insane. Pentex tried to put them down, but they failed when the Bloodlicks proved to be able to split into swarms of bats. Now the Bloodlicks wage an endless war against both Wyrm and Gaian forces, and will only settle upon one side once Bat has.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Grondr come the Hogzillas, a very successful Mockery Breed using modern day boars and pigs. All very fat no matter the form, they are the exact opposite of the Grondr in function. Where the Grondr cleansed spiritual areas, the Hogzillas defile the land. They radiate an aura of uncleanness, and Pentex creates them frequently, even if they are unpleasant to be around. The only problem is that the Skull Pigs, upon encountering Hogzillas, will attack them to the exckusion of all else. Even if there is a raging Garou pack bearing down on them, the Skull Pigs will focus there full effort on killing the Hogzillas.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Khara come the Saber Maws, a successful mockery breed often deployed alongside the Kerasi. They posess a strange ability to grow bones from there bodies and even manipulate the bones of others.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Okuma come the savage Aku-Kuma, this mockery is perverted, lazy, gluttonous, and blood thirsty. Despite the wyrm taint in there souls, they have a cute and cuddly animal form. Pentex uses them in various showbussiness ventures such as zoo displays, tv shows, and other concerns. The Aku-Kuma love to corrupt young kids, which is exactly what Pentex has them do. In spite of this, there loyalty to the company is completely dependent on the company providing them the depths of sleaze and vice that can be accessed by fame and money. The company is more than happy to provide it, but that could change.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Ao Varna come the Terror-pins, a powerful breed perfectly suited to various tactics that Pentex could once not acess. They are masters of manipulating memory and the Mnesis, and are also able to manipulate the elements. One of there favorite tactics is to manipulate dreams, turning them into advertisements for Pentex products. They also plant false memories of betrayal in the companies foes, delighting when raging Garou slaughter each other over a false memory.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">From the Ratkin Bards come the Pipers, and unlike most mockery breeds they do not originate from Pentex. Instead they arise from an old Wyrm cult from mideval times, with Pentex finding the methods to make them in the modern day. The Pipers mo is like that of the famous pied piper, ie they drive a plague of vermin to a town and offer to get rid of it for a price. The plague will be bad enough that they accept, and once the plague is gone one of two things will happen. One is that the town will willingly stiff the Piper out of greed or poverty. The other is that the town will pay the piper, but the Piper will up the prize to ridicoulus levels that the town will refuse to pay. Either way, the Piper retailiates by stealing all the children of the town, using there pipes to lure them just as they lure vermin and banes. The fate of the children is horrible, as those with even a trace of Kinfolk blood in them are given to the various Wyrm Shapeshifters, much as the Ratkin kinfolk were taken by the Garou. The rest are taken to Malfeas to become slaves, sacrified to uncaring Banes, or other more nightmarish fates.<br /> <br /> -------------- </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When a Changing Breed goes extinct or is otherwise lost, the Wyrm seals away the fallen members of there breed in a stasis alongside other forgotten horrors such as the Midnight Shadows and the fallen Grondr (who will be identical to the Hogzillas, as Skull Pigs are not technically shapeshifters any more). But once the Apocalypse is in full swing, the Wyrm is going to crack open those seals and let the long forgotten monsters out, letting the fallen Nagah slither out and the Xibalbans fly once more.<br /> <br /> ------------------ </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Ratkin in the modern day are basically the Skaven, being corrupted by the Wyld and having various Wyld-tainted splinter totems of Rat that are all inspired by the faces of the Great Horned Rat.<br /> <br /> ----------------- </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The deception of the Nagah is not complete. They have a presence in the Beast Courts, and rumors of snake shifters exist in many places. Since banes can not possess them, the fallen Nagah are sealed away by the Wyrm, but there continued existence means no Mockery Breed can be made from there remains.<br /> <br /> --------------------- </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">My next post will be on the fallen breeds from the Fera that don\u2019t have them, as well as an idea on the Simba. But what you think of this stuff?</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T05:59:35-07:00","id":1518926,"title":"","content":"I like the ideas, personally I wouldn't have so many as having been created as its nice for the Wyrm to have to have difficulty in overcoming the natural order to twist it.<br /> Depending on how you view Gaia in the modern days (absent, domant, in so much pain she's helpless or conserving her energy), the latter being supported by the continued creation of Kami, I can see her efforts being directed to stopping the perversion of her fallen children.<br /> <br /> I can see Kami being created specifically to stop the corruption and rare fallen breed ancestor spirits desperatey trying to save themselves and whatever remnants are kept in statis.<br /> The potential perversion of the Apis or Grondr might even be enough of a tipping point where Bull or Boar appeal to their Garou packs and force the ancestor spirits to inform them of whats at stake, it has the makings of a great campaign.<br /> Considering that they will act as Pack Totems for the Garou despite teh destruction fo their children (perhaps they act on Gaias instruction).<br /> <br /> I also like th idea that the Wyrm is often its own worst enemy, in its corrupter incarnation it relishes and promotes suspicion, fear, paranoia etc, the Black Spiral Dancers are unlikely to welcome further Mockery Breeds, they are the apex predators of the corrupter, riddled with delusions and insecurities, I can easily see them stopping such attempts to bring more changers back.<br /> After all their reasoning could be if attention is drawn to bringing the fallen back what stops Gaia doing the same, might this little revelation give some humans or even pragmatic Glass Walkers or Children of Gaia a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Now if modern science could simply solve the low reproductive rate of the garou they might have already done it, but that dosen't stop the BSDs from fearing that too much attention on bringing these races back might lead to advances they don't want.<br /> I also like the internal warring that Wyrm factions commit on each other, internecine conflict between Pentax companys, cults v pentax, BSDs v BSDs etc, the wyem isn't a unified force quite the opposite it revels in chaos and artbitary destruction.<br /> <br /> Finally I also like the idea that some of the fallen ancestors spirits have become banes and thus created their own forms of Formori\u200b <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> has a really good Vampire Bat Formori derived from the Dresden Files Red Court vampires, I like them as the successors of the <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Camazotz</span>\u200b.<br /> <br /> Really good ideas though, given me lots to think about","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 07-27-2023, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T13:04:45-07:00","id":1518953,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27824_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27824\" data-vbnamecard=\"27824\">Arcanus</a> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, thanks for your kind words, and now heres the next post.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">More headcanons and homebrews</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Inspired by the W20 Baset Breedbook, I think that the Simba are in a pecarcarious position. While Black Tooth is dead, his followers are mostly alive. If the Simba allow there pride and the manipulation of the former members of the Endless Storm to lead them into the Wyrms corruption, then the Simba will become the Scarred.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Scarred are to the Bastet what the Black Spiral Dancers are to the Garou. All are servants of the newest Bane Totem, that being Holo the Rhinoceros Lord, and the Simba Homeland will become a new Wyrm Realm like the Spiral Homeland. The Scarred Realm, as there homeland is now known, enters a permanent night, a symbol of Helios retracting his blessing.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">To become one of the Scarred, one must endure a hunt upon the savanah of the Scarred Realm while banes, wyrmish monstrosities, and the Scarred all hunt them. This is the fate of all captured Bastet, and the only way to survive is to accept Cahlash as ones truest lord and master.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">At the hunts end, the new Scarred earns there name, making a lasting scar on there body using either Silver or Gold (if Simba aren\u2019t vunerable to Gold, a sign of Helios turning on them). Only true Simba can gain a leadership position, and the Scarred target there uncorrupted breatheren above all others, for not all Simba fell.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The hellcats and Histpah still exist, but they quickly become subdivisions of the Scarred.<br /> <br /> ------------------ </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now the fallen breeds for those who don\u2019t have them. I will count skull pigs for Grondr, and fallen Gurhal are in the MET book of the wyrm</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Apis who fell to the Wyrm became the Moloch. Like the ancient god whose name they take, the fallen Apis revel in killing children and using fire, or rather Balefire, to kill those who oppose them. Unlike the modern day Minotaur Mockery Breed, the Kao have full acess to the charms and magics that allow the Apis to be Gaia\u2019s matchmakers, and they use these powers to great effect.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In the ancient times, the Moloch would create entire vilages devoted to worshiping them, and would often sacrifice the unfit children to bane totems and heads of the hydra. These blasphemous villages attracted Gaian defenders, but the defenders were powerful formori who through twisted magics bred true. The Moloch are now in stasis like the Xibalbans, but they left one last curse upon the foes of the Wyrm. They pooled there magics together to create the Minotaur Bane totem, and now slumber awaiting the Wyrms call at the end of days.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The fallen kitsune exist in two types. The first is the Kyuubi No Akuma created by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1645\" data-vbnamecard=\"1645\">Autochthon</a>, found here (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/701895-kyuubi-no-akuma-those-who-have-lost-faith\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...ave-lost-faith</a>).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But there exists another breed, one that is truly devoted to the Wyrm, and is known to exist among the kitsune that exist outside of the middle kingdom (for they do exist, just hidden like most Fera who do not live in the Beast Courts). They are the Huli Jing, and they are no cowards like the devil foxes who sell themselves to the thousand hells.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">While the reason for there fall may vary (a great many decry the unfairness of the curse), when the kitsune who becomes a Huli Jing falls, they fall to the elemental Wyrms. Where they were once tied to the elements of Gaia, now they tie themselves to the pollution of the Wyrm. They serve the Elemental Wyrms proper, and care only for there dark goal of replacing all the elements of Gaia with there Wyrmish counterparts, though they will obey the elemental majein and with other heads of the hydra, a few even having positions in Pentex and its subsidiaries as consultants, possessing a much better relationship with the company than the black spiral dancers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Huli Jing paths keep the names of there uncorrupted kin as a calculated insult, but the elements are very different. All are nightmarish, and the kin of Renard (as kitsune are often called outside of the middle kingdom) must fight the fallen with all there might. Each path has a nickname that is more commonly used.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Eji of the Wyrm, known as the Mutators, are warriors who love to kill in gruesome wayxs, of which there are many by the usage of there element of Ooze. A combination of Sludge and Balefire, it is a powerful mutagenic substance that functions much like mutagens do in science fiction works, but also with horrible side effects. A normal human exposed to the Ooze become nightmares unimagined as trace amounts of animal DNA are unlocked, creating things like a Fomor or a shifter that lives its short life in constant agony, or has junk DNA unlocked to make things Gaia never meant to occur. The supernatural fare even worse, as the Ooze makes even more extreme mutations out of the unnatural powers. Even spirits are not safe from the Ooze, as Pattern Spiders soon gain elements of things like rats or scorpions or what have you. Not even Banes are safe, but these wyrmish spirits endure the mutations very well. Pity the kinfolk who is exposed to the Ooze, as they soon become a chimera of nightmarish proportions as every shifter bloodline, no matter how distant, manifests at once, possibly resulting in a thing that has the muzzle of a wolf, the wings of a bat, the legs of a giant spider, and the gills of a shark.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Doshi of the Wyrm, known as Smokers, are magic weavers that use the element of Smoke. A combination of Smog and Balefire, the element of Smoke is gaseous poison in all its forms. The Smokers inflict lung cancer and horrible diseases upon all who challenge them. Not even the Garou can fight at full strength when there lungs have been reduced to a lump of charcoal.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Gukutsushi of the Wyrm, known as Trippers, are illusionists much like there Gaian counterparts, but they create there illusions through the element of Intoxicant. The Trippers combine Toxin and Smog to create and secrete drugs and alcohol at every instant. Each breath they take comes out as cigarette or vape smoke, there claws hollow like needles and inject heroin, and there tail drip hallucinogens. There toxins can affect any being, and they love to addict the changing breeds to unique drugs only the Wyrm can provide them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Kataribe of the Wyrm, known as the Slick, are not storytellers but saboteurs, using the element of Oil to slip in anywhere and destroy morale. The blasphemous child of Sludge and Toxins, Oil is perhaps the strongest of the combination Wyrm elements that the Huli Jing embody and advance, for it is so ubiquitious. More pain and Wyrm Taint have had Oil at there source than any other, and the Slick work to keep it that way. They are experts at slipping past defenses and committing sabotage of all types, from assassination to destruction of knowledge and beyond.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I\u2019m gonna have to do my fallen Nagah ideas another time, but I want peoples thoughts on this stuff.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T07:28:12-07:00","id":1519247,"title":"","content":"double post<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":". 07-31-2023, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T08:08:42-07:00","id":1519251,"title":"","content":"I do feel it's important to play up the fact that neither Blacktooth nor the Endless Storm were servitors of the Wyrm. They were horrible, amoral people willing to do anything, but they were fighting the Wyrm and keeping it under wraps. They were what would have happened if the worst tendencies of the Red Talons and the Shadow Lords took over the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Some of them falling to the Wyrm after losing their leader and falling out of favour seems reasonable, but at the end of the day, most would just retreat to their teritorries and political realities would force Ahadi to open discussions with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T08:55:50-07:00","id":1519255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519251#post1519251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel it's important to play up the fact that neither Blacktooth nor the Endless Storm were servitors of the Wyrm. They were horrible, amoral people willing to do anything, but they were fighting the Wyrm and keeping it under wraps. They were what would have happened if the worst tendencies of the Red Talons and the Shadow Lords took over the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Some of them falling to the Wyrm after losing their leader and falling out of favour seems reasonable, but at the end of the day, most would just retreat to their teritorries and political realities would force Ahadi to open discussions with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>i totally agree with that. The Scarred are what i think would happen to the Simba if the events presented in the W20 Bastet Breedbook happen. Admittedly i am uncertain if its canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T09:01:26-07:00","id":1519257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519255#post1519255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i totally agree with that. The Scarred are what i think would happen to the Simba if the events presented in the W20 Bastet Breedbook happen. Admittedly i am uncertain if its canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Bastet Breedbook? Uh, do you mean the Changing Breeds 20th? There wasn't a 20th Anniversary Bastet breedbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T09:26:10-07:00","id":1519260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519257#post1519257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 Bastet Breedbook? Uh, do you mean the Changing Breeds 20th? There wasn't a 20th Anniversary Bastet breedbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, its definitely non canon. the link is here <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/373077/Bastet-Breedbook?term=bastet\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ok?term=bastet</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":