y\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519262#post1519262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, that makes much more sense. Thanks for clearing it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>you are very welcome. I'm glad we sorted this out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:02:26-07:00","id":1519268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a> good ideas, I like the idea of the Scarred although I\u2019d have them as the Bastet version of the BSDs in general, in my mind equally applicable to fallen Balam.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Simba I can see hardline elements of the Endless Storm falling with Blacktooths death and a civil war of sorts starting particularly if you follow the W20 (unofficial) Bastet book in the non-corrupted trying to purge the Scarred before they release the great Bane.<br /> <br /> The Bastet are interesting in seeing the Wyrm in its balance form albeit a dark seductive version, so it makes me wonder if the Corrupter tricks them by pretending to be Cahlash, but prefer the Scarred to Hellcats.<br /> <br /> Moloch\u2019s I like although they\u2019d be rare to survive the War of Rage, but they fit the mythological Minotaur (the misshapen adopted son of Minos was meant to be a man eater hence the sacrifice of maidens).<br /> <br /> Kitsune I\u2019m in two minds, there\u2019s something niggling me about Gaias youngest children, the fact they burst into flame if a kindred tries to embrace them.<br /> I wonder if this goes further not full resistance to the Centipede but do they die or get stripped of the Fox if they turn to the Yomi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:53:32-07:00","id":1519274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519268#post1519268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26173\" data-vbnamecard=\"26173\">evtrax</a> good ideas, I like the idea of the Scarred although I\u2019d have them as the Bastet version of the BSDs in general, in my mind equally applicable to fallen Balam.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Simba I can see hardline elements of the Endless Storm falling with Blacktooths death and a civil war of sorts starting particularly if you follow the W20 (unofficial) Bastet book in the non-corrupted trying to purge the Scarred before they release the great Bane.<br /> <br /> The Bastet are interesting in seeing the Wyrm in its balance form albeit a dark seductive version, so it makes me wonder if the Corrupter tricks them by pretending to be Cahlash, but prefer the Scarred to Hellcats.<br /> <br /> Moloch\u2019s I like although they\u2019d be rare to survive the War of Rage, but they fit the mythological Minotaur (the misshapen adopted son of Minos was meant to be a man eater hence the sacrifice of maidens).<br /> <br /> Kitsune I\u2019m in two minds, there\u2019s something niggling me about Gaias youngest children, the fact they burst into flame if a kindred tries to embrace them.<br /> I wonder if this goes further not full resistance to the Centipede but do they die or get stripped of the Fox if they turn to the Yomi.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scarred are the Bastet version of the BSDs. Its just the simba form the core of the tribe, like how the fallen White Howlers form the core of the BSDs.<br /> <br /> Thats a great story idea, and it pulls from the apocalypse prelude for the Bastet from time of judgement.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if its not the corrupter pretending to be Cahlash, idk what it is.<br /> <br /> I didnt think the Moloch's are really around post War of Rage, having gone into stasis like the Xibalbans. But maybe there are isolated villages that worship an ancient surviving Moloch still around. and of course the Minotaur was the biggest inspiration for fallen Apis, but since the mockery breed was the Minotaur, i had to use something else as the main basis. Moloch was actually not my first choice, i was going to use Kao (a minotaur equivelent from Indian myth). <br /> <br /> I did not know that about the Kitsune, thats cool. <br /> <br /> Maybe the process of becoming a Huli Jing requires the Kitsune to die, with the power of the Wyrm resuructing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T13:28:29-07:00","id":1519279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519274#post1519274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to use Kao (a minotaur equivelent from Indian myth).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats sounds interesting, I\u2019ll look the Kao up<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519274#post1519274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know that about the Kitsune, thats cool.<br /> <br /> Maybe the process of becoming a Huli Jing requires the Kitsune to die, with the power of the Wyrm resuructing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it could be that only through the intervention of the Yama Kings (which could be Wyrm Maejin Incarna), in ritually killing a Kitsune that they are pledged into dark service.<br /> <br /> Alternative Wyrm auspices could be based on the Yomi worlds (if you use KOTE)<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T13:35:57-07:00","id":1519280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519279#post1519279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats sounds interesting, I\u2019ll look the Kao up<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well it could be that only through the intervention of the Yama Kings (which could be Wyrm Maejin Incarna), in ritually killing a Kitsune that they are pledged into dark service.<br /> <br /> Alternative Wyrm auspices could be based on the Yomi worlds (if you use KOTE)<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>ok then. But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1645\" data-vbnamecard=\"1645\">Autochthon</a> already made the kitsune who sell themselves to the yama kings. The Huli Jing are a different breed, especially considering that they will actively fight for the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T14:28:34-07:00","id":1519284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519280#post1519280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ok then. But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1645\" data-vbnamecard=\"1645\">Autochthon</a> already made the kitsune who sell themselves to the yama kings. The Huli Jing are a different breed, especially considering that they will actively fight for the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far enough, I do like the idea of them being sacrificed to the Maejin.<br /> <br /> On a Homebrew note never agreed with the Kitsune not regenerating (outside of Gifts), comparatively Bubasti have the similar Magical capability and longevity but still regenerate, and Paper Magic isn\u2019t that powerful until Rank 4 and above. <br /> <br /> I have the Kitsune able to regenerate in Dragon Nests or other places of high Yang Chi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:47:54-07:00","id":1519293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519284#post1519284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Far enough, I do like the idea of them being sacrificed to the Maejin.<br /> <br /> On a Homebrew note never agreed with the Kitsune not regenerating (outside of Gifts), comparatively Bubasti have the similar Magical capability and longevity but still regenerate, and Paper Magic isn\u2019t that powerful until Rank 4 and above.<br /> <br /> I have the Kitsune able to regenerate in Dragon Nests or other places of high Yang Chi.</div> </div> </div> </div>thats a good idea. I didnt know about the not regenerating thing, but i always assumed they were squishy wizatds, but more like nuwisha or Corax. IE they arent meant to be fighting Garou straight up, but they arent going to die because of bullets (unless they are silver bullets). <br /> <br /> Of course, Huli Jing are tougher, though they rely upon there Wyrmish elements and dirty tricks more than endurance/regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T03:01:59-07:00","id":1519322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514065-head-canons-home-brew-part-2?p=1519293#post1519293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thats a good idea. I didnt know about the not regenerating thing, but i always assumed they were squishy wizatds, but more like nuwisha or Corax. IE they arent meant to be fighting Garou straight up, but they arent going to die because of bullets (unless they are silver bullets).<br /> <br /> Of course, Huli Jing are tougher, though they rely upon there Wyrmish elements and dirty tricks more than endurance/regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they're pretty comparable to the Bubasti (stat wise) who have pretty much the same benefits and arcane range, however the Bubasti have no lack of regeneration, Kitsune on the other hand treat all damage as aggravated and heal as per a mortal (so by that definition is not even 1 point of aggravated healed per day), granted they can soak everything bar silver.<br /> <br /> Paper Magic is good but its essentially a range of gifts which aren't in themselves that different, novel or powerful (bar the Gnosis storage), plus Hedge Magic/Sorcery is good but not quick, its not about power gaming but there has to be an element of suvivability in werewolf (the other aspect being its unlikely its a whole pack or kit of Kitsune, so you'll probably be with other changers which will put you in combat situations (as much as you avoid them)).<br /> <br /> Its also goes against the warrior auspice, even if they follow a shadow warrior/assassin path they're inevitably going to come into a tooth and claw scenario, once or twice which could be fatal, given that most Wyrm creatures inflict Aggravated damage off the bat.<br /> <br /> I'd draw on myth and tie Fox regeneration to allow it but it in sacred places, good chi, needing Green Jade (Jade is associated with purification, luck and some colours with healing) or I'd give the Kitsune something else that makes them distinct, their Soak is stronger (perhaps they add their Tails to their stamina) which links to their quicksilver nature and not everything is as it seems, an innate higher level of magic resistance (above Nightfolk Countermagic) or resistance to corruption (which themically ties to their being the youngest children of the Emerald Mother, so designed with a different purpose).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 08-01-2023, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T11:44:48-07:00","id":1519352,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27824_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27824\" data-vbnamecard=\"27824\">Arcanus</a>, I did not know that about Kitsune. It is now my headcanon that they do not treat everything as aggravated damage, they have some more resistance/soak, enough to not just be shredded like an average human going up against a shifter or other monster, and heal like a mortal most of the time, but when spending whatever power shifters use to trigger healing they can heal faster, and they can do it at reduced cost in the circumstances you describe.<br /> <br /> Of course the Huli Jing have a different thing. It\u2019s the same for them, but when they suffer aggravated wounds they can turn there blood into whatever wyrmish element they represent. Mechanically it does a bit of damage, and depends on which element they represent. Ooze causes radiation/mutation, Smoke causes fire damage, Intoxicant messes with the mind, and oil does damage by being ignited by the attack.<br /> <br /> The Huli Jing require defiled places, obsidian (the opposite of jade), and/or a place that is rich in the Wyrm\u2019s energy when triggering the immense fast healing.<br /> -------------- <br /> <br /> Heres the fallen Nagah and some more homebrews/headcanons<br /> <br /> The fallen Nagah known as the Vritra, or the Drought Kings. They are not the Crown of India and Africa but take the name to both mock the loyal Nagah and to spread more dissent among the changing breeds, hoping the Garou will slaughter the loyal Nagah crown out of mistaken identity much as the Bunyip were slain. The human memories of the Drought Kings have permanently associated the word Vritra with drought.<br /> <br /> The Drought Kings almost always fall to the Wyrm through there Ananata, the den-realm that all Nagah have. The Ananata is naturally full of water, but somehow those of the Nagah who become the Drought Kings are drained dry. How this happens varies, but when it does and if the Nagah survives the loss (given it usually happens violently) and the subsiquint hunting by the other Nagah (as they recognize the wrongness of a drained Ananata), drives them to the Wyrms service, as being deprived of the connection to the sacred element of water drives the Nagah utterly mad.<br /> <br /> Drought Kings wage an eternal shadow war upon the Nagah, taking every opportunity to mock there still loyal counterparts. While most Drought Kings are solitary, when a Nest is formed it is always three Drought Kings, each representing a Triantic Wyrm head. Those who serve the Beast of War are savage brutes, those who serve the Eater of Souls are gluttinous and wasteful, and those of the Defiler are cunning and scheming.<br /> <br /> The Drought Kings as a whole serve Atlacoya, a Bane totem of Strength. Once a Gaian Incarna of drought, she was one of the first totems to be corrupted by the Wyrm. Atlacoya seeks to reduce all of reality to naught but a dry plain and watch as the few survivors vicously fight over what little food and water remains. Like Ammit\u2019s realm, the drought stricken plains that serve as Atlacoya\u2019s realm are isolated from the rest of Malfeas, but unlike Ammit Atlacoya does not have plans to reestablish those ties. No, instead she is focused on her plan to reduce Mexico and South America (which is the place that her realm connects to in the material world) into a drought stricken wasteland.<br /> <br /> Atlacoya also gives her blessing to the Black Spiral Dancers, and Bastards who follow Atlacoya never need water or hydration and can cause dehydration in others. The ban is particularly damaging, for it decrees that they must never let blood water the ground. Her servants masters of harming without spilling blood as a result.<br /> <br /> --------- <br /> <br /> Heres the general stuff<br /> <br /> This is probably canon, but I see the entire Triat as utterly insane and hostile to reality. If the Garou managed to defeat the Wyrm and completely remove its influence, then the Weaver or the Wyld would quickly replace it as the apocalypse causing threat.<br /> <br /> -------------- <br /> <br /> Apophis from the Midnight Circus and the main antagonist of Mummy the Resurrection is actually a head of the Hydra/Corrupted Wyrm. It would have been the fourth of the Triatic Wyrm heads, but something happened to make it the most independent of the heads, even able to slither out on its own into the deep umbra.<br /> <br /> Apophis is also the Hydra\u2019s back up plan. Should the Garou or some other force somehow manage to do the impossible and destroy the Hydra, then Apophis would quickly grow in size, power, and heads to become a new Corruptor Wyrm. This new Wyrm would be even more powerful than the original, because unlike the original it can move in the Umbra instead of being bound by the Weavers webs.<br /> <br /> The only way to avoid this scenario is to free the true Wyrm, the Balance Wyrm\u2019s freedom would destroy the Hydra entirely and force both Weaver and Wyld back into balance.<br /> <br /> -------------- <br /> <br /> Queen Ananasa and Gaia are both extremely overestimated by the Changing Breeds. Yes they are both extremely powerful spirits, even by Celestine standards, but they are not equal or superiors to the Triat.<br /> <br /> -------------- <br /> <br /> The Yama Kings, like most vampires, do not actively serve the Wyrm. Oh sure, they do the work of the corrupter, but so do a great many humans.<br /> <br /> --------------- <br /> <br /> The phenomenon of Skin Dancers/Skin Walkers has existed since the Banestorm back in prehistory. The skin dancer tribe of Samuel Haight is merely a recent version and made prominent by the urban legend status of Haight. It is not just Garou either, as technically the rites can be adapted for any shifter. A great example of this exists in the Raven Mockers, skin dancers of the Corax.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T04:40:31-07:00","id":1519841,"title":"","content":"Hauglosk (or the anti hanaro) exists, but as a state that is similar to Hanaro. It's been a major factor in many of the Garous (and the Feras) worst atrocities, making things like the wars of rage, tears, and shame so much worse. <br /> <br /> It's not an instant loosing your character stayed, and can be broken out of. However, it is harder to break out of than Hanaro because its harder to detect and is at times not seen as something to get rid of. <br /> <br /> The Red Talons for instance are almost always in a state of Hauglosk, and they really dont want to be otherwise. <br /> <br /> \u2010----\u2010---------- <br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers (and other fallen Fera) can fall to Hanaro and Hauglosk. However the source of these feelings is different than there uncorrupted counterparts. <br /> <br /> Wyrm Hanaro comes from the seemingly endless war agaisnt Gaia. Yes the BSD's believe that the Wyrm has already won, but the fact that the Garou seem to not realize that truth no matter what can cause the fallen shifter to go into something approximating Hanaro. <br /> <br /> Wyrm Hauglosk comes from an unholy determination to kill the last struggling defenders of Gaia and finally end the farce that is the endless war agaisnt the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}